---
const { prefix = '' } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="thesis argument-block" aria-labelledby={`${prefix}thesis-heading`}>
  <p class="eyebrow">Our approach</p>
  <h2 id={`${prefix}thesis-heading`}>What is the role of testing?</h2>
  <p class="intro">
    Testing, benchmarking, and red-teaming are crucial for finding failures, but tests cannot
    establish that important classes of problems are absent.
  </p>
  <ul class="three-questions" role="list">
    <li>Which properties can we guarantee?</li>
    <li>Under which assumptions?</li>
    <li>Where do guarantees end?</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="scope-note">
    <h3>Scope and limits</h3>
    <p>
      We seek analyzable guarantees for specified properties under stated assumptions—not proof that
      an entire AI system is safe. A proof can establish that a mechanism meets an objective. It
      cannot, by itself, tell us that we chose the right objective or that its assumptions hold in
      deployment.
    </p>
    <p>Formal analysis complements empirical evaluation and alignment research.</p>
  </div>
</section>
